course: dictionary
lesson: 16061
title: Vocally: using your voice
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Vocally comes from voice. It tells you how something is done: with the voice, out loud, so others can hear. «The crowd vocally cheered when the team scored.» The cheering was loud and open, so everyone could hear how they felt.
explain: The word often goes with protest or support. «Mum was vocally against the new bus route» means she said so loudly and openly, not in secret. Look for clues in the sentence such as cheered, shouted, sang or complained.
explain: In music, vocally means using the singing voice. «The song is very hard vocally» means the singer's voice has a tough job, not the drums or the piano. Ask yourself: is this about speaking or singing?
fact: Vocally means by speaking out loudly and openly, so others clearly hear your opinion.
fact: Vocally also means using the voice, especially in singing.
fact: The root of vocally is voice, so if you can hear it, it is often vocal.
fact: Common phrases are "vocally opposed to", "vocally support" and "very vocally".
fact: A good check is to swap in "out loud" or "with my voice" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The parents spoke vocally at the meeting, and everyone heard them.» What does vocally mean here? | By sleeping through the meeting | By writing a letter quietly | By staying silent and still | *By speaking out loudly and openly
exercise: «Mia sang vocally in the school choir.» What does vocally mean here? | By drawing a picture | *With her voice, singing | Quietly in her head | Using her hands only
exercise: «Sam was vocally opposed to the plan, so he shouted his no at every meeting.» What does vocally suggest? | He agreed with it happily | *Openly, so everyone can hear his view | He did not care about the plan | Secretly, in a whisper
test: «The fans cheered vocally when their team scored.» What does vocally mean? | *Loudly, using their voices | By dancing without a sound | Angrily, by throwing things | Silently, with their eyes closed
test: «Ella was vocally supportive of her friend's idea.» What does vocally show? | She sang a song about it at night | She did not support the idea | *She spoke out clearly to back her friend | She kept her support a secret
exam: A teacher asks, «Did Jo speak vocally in the debate?» What does she mean? | Did Jo leave the room early? | *Did Jo speak out openly and clearly? | Did Jo sit quietly with no opinion? | Did Jo write a note instead?
